00:03:13.796 --> 00:03:17.316
Right. And beside the scene the agent is going to.

00:03:17.356 --> 00:03:23.796
Run through multiple loops of that react
pattern we just talked about and return a reply.

00:03:24.716 --> 00:03:29.196
Let's see how it works. So the agent receives the message from Terry.

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:34.196
Now it starts its first iteration of that react loop.

00:03:34.916 --> 00:03:40.036
It pulls the system prompt.
It's something like you are a insurance agent.

00:03:41.036 --> 00:03:44.076
And now it also pulls Terry’s preferences.

00:03:44.276 --> 00:03:48.356
The conversation histories. And this is the memory step.

00:03:49.156 --> 00:03:56.076
Right now the agent format a prompt based
on all those memory states into a prompt

00:03:56.476 --> 00:03:59.196
and send it to the large language model to reason.

00:03:59.796 --> 00:04:02.476
And this is the reasoning step we just talked about.

00:04:04.036 --> 00:04:11.316
Now ARM decides I have the request context,
but I don't know any details about the driver.

00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:18.956
So it decides to call a tool,
get driver details, and come back to Terry's name,

00:04:19.116 --> 00:04:23.996
his license numbers and the driving histories.

00:04:24.836 --> 00:04:29.716
Right. So you see, this is a small loop of the react.

00:04:30.156 --> 00:04:36.596
What it did is it remember your reasons and your act, right?

